From 6087f6b26fec84a417ff569e3e709a25db774b90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:41:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/35] Reverb: Modulation (depth, default 0: still) and
 Pre-delay (0 to 100 ms)

A held tone wobbled in the reverb: the modulated delays of the Mutable model (since v10 at
Mutable Instruments' speed, 16 times the speed of 1.2.1) and of the Digital plate move its
level by about 16 dB and its pitch by 5 cents (Mutable) or 16 dB and 19 cents (Digital),
measured on a held 220 Hz tone. That's also much of the washed-out sound of the tail.

- Modulation (Reverb menu, song and sound, 0 to 50, not for Freeverb): the depth of the
  modulated delays and of Mutable's smear. 0, the default, keeps the reverb still, a held tone
  stays within 0.2 dB. 50 is the depth of v10 to v13, bit for bit. Songs without the attribute
  load with 0; saved as "modulation" (Q31) in the reverb element.
- Pre-delay (0 to 100 ms, all models): a delay before the reverb, so the dry sound stands on
  its own before the reverb sets in. Saved as "preDelay" (ms). 0 leaves the input untouched;
  switched on, the delay starts empty. 17.6 KB of RAM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
